WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:11.729
The White Rabbit soon noticed Alice hunting for his gloves and fan.

2
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.338
He called out to her in an angry voice.

3
00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:19.294
"Mary Ann, what are you doing here?

4
00:00:19.295 --> 00:00:27.139
Run home right now, and fetch me a pair of gloves and a fan! Hurry!"

5
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:31.644
Alice knew that the rabbit had mistaken her for someone else.

6
00:00:31.645 --> 00:00:37.085
But he sounded so angry that she ran where he was pointing.

7
00:00:37.086 --> 00:00:40.032
She didn't try to explain his mistake to him.

8
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:44.244
"He probably thinks I'm his servant," she thought.

9
00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:47.055
"He'll be surprised when he finds out who I am.

10
00:00:47.056 --> 00:00:53.630
But he's so angry right now that I'd better find his gloves and fan."

11
00:00:53.631 --> 00:00:57.558
Alice soon came upon a neat little house.

12
00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:02.577
On the door was a brass sign that said W. Rabbit.

13
00:01:02.578 --> 00:01:08.083
She hurried inside and closed the front door.

14
00:01:08.084 --> 00:01:13.401
"How strange to be sent on an errand by a rabbit." Alice laughed.

15
00:01:13.402 --> 00:01:19.943
"Soon Dinah will be sending me on errands too!"

16
00:01:19.944 --> 00:01:23.445
Alice entered a room with a table near the window.

17
00:01:23.446 --> 00:01:27.467
On the table lay a fan and a pair of white gloves.

18
00:01:27.468 --> 00:01:32.088
Alice picked them up.

19
00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:40.671
She was about to leave when she spotted a bottle on the floor.

20
00:01:40.672 --> 00:01:47.017
This time there was no label saying, Drink Me, but Alice uncorked the bottle anyway.

21
00:01:47.018 --> 00:01:53.324
"Whenever I eat or drink anything today, something interesting happens," she thought.

22
00:01:53.325 --> 00:01:56.262
She took a sip.

23
00:01:56.263 --> 00:02:01.163
"I hope this will make me grow again because I'm tired of being so small."

24
00:02:01.164 --> 00:02:06.702
That is exactly what happened and much faster than Alice expected.

25
00:02:06.703 --> 00:02:12.147
Before she had drunk half the bottle, her head was pressing against the ceiling.

26
00:02:12.148 --> 00:02:14.657
She quickly put down the bottle.

27
00:02:14.658 --> 00:02:20.365
"That's enough! I hope I won't grow anymore because I can't get out the door.

28
00:02:20.366 --> 00:02:23.018
I wish I hadn't drunk so much."

29
00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:25.126
But it was too late for that.

30
00:02:25.127 --> 00:02:29.793
Alice went on growing and soon had to kneel on the floor.

31
00:02:29.794 --> 00:02:33.987
In another minute she had to lie with one foot up the chimney.

32
00:02:33.988 --> 00:02:36.888
She stuck one arm out the window.

33
00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:40.769
"There's no more room for me!" Alice wailed.

34
00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.303
Luckily she stopped growing.

35
00:02:43.304 --> 00:02:48.783
But she was very uncomfortable, being squashed inside the White Rabbit's house.

36
00:02:48.784 --> 00:02:52.456
"It was much nicer at home," Alice said.

37
00:02:52.457 --> 00:02:57.863
"I wasn't always changing size, and mice and rabbits weren't ordering me around.

38
00:02:57.864 --> 00:03:00.710
I wish I hadn't gone down that rabbit hole.

39
00:03:00.711 --> 00:03:05.606
And yet . . . and yet . . . this is quite an adventure.

40
00:03:05.607 --> 00:03:08.388
I used to think fairy tales weren't real.

41
00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:12.025
And now I seem to be in the middle of one!

42
00:03:12.026 --> 00:03:15.492
Maybe someone will write a book about me—"

43
00:03:15.493 --> 00:03:21.006
Suddenly Alice heard an angry voice outside.

44
00:03:21.007 --> 00:03:29.524
"Mary Ann, where are you!" the White Rabbit called.

45
00:03:29.525 --> 00:03:39.624
He tried to open his front door, but Alice's elbow was pressing hard against it.

46
00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:44.901
"Then I'll go through a window," the White Rabbit said.

47
00:03:44.902 --> 00:03:47.947
"No, you won't," Alice said.

48
00:03:47.948 --> 00:03:52.144
She waited until she heard the White Rabbit under the window.

49
00:03:52.145 --> 00:03:55.156
Then she tried to grab him.

50
00:03:55.157 --> 00:04:01.437
The White Rabbit shrieked and ran away.

51
00:04:01.438 --> 00:04:06.896
"Pat! Pat! Where are you?"

52
00:04:06.897 --> 00:04:12.386
"Right here! Digging potatoes in the garden," a man replied.

53
00:04:12.387 --> 00:04:20.220
"Pat, what's that in the window?"

54
00:04:20.221 --> 00:04:28.562
There was a pause while the gardener looked at the house.

55
00:04:28.563 --> 00:04:32.652
"Hmm . . . Looks like an arm to me."

56
00:04:32.653 --> 00:04:39.510
"An arm? Who's ever seen an arm that big? Take it away!"

57
00:04:39.511 --> 00:04:43.667
Alice waved her arm around and heard some whispering.

58
00:04:43.668 --> 00:04:52.634
Then all was silent for a while—until a crowd began gathering under the window.

